error[ffi_parameter_type]: `x` of `narrow` is declared wider than the header's `int` — clang read the header, and C would convert the value in silence
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2137-a-call-behind-a-counting-macro-moves-no-value.hero:12:5
     |
  12 |     function narrow(x: i64) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: §4.19: a result may be wider than C's, and a parameter is declared at the header's own width and sign. Declare it `i32`, and convert at the call where the value is known to fit
  fix (guess): declare it `i32`

error[ffi_constant_type]: `K_DIV` in `fixedbugs-2137-counted-call.h` cannot be declared `i64`: clang refuses the header's value at line 7: its expression holds an operation C leaves undefined for the operands it is given, and the program's own unit, built with clang's checks for an overflow, a shift, a division by zero and a float out of an integer's range, traps where it reads it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2137-a-call-behind-a-counting-macro-moves-no-value.hero:14:5
     |
  14 |     constant K_DIV: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2137-counted-call.h` line 7 reads `#define K_DIV ((-2147483647 - 1) / -1)`
  note: an operation C leaves undefined gives no value: wherever C computes it, a program reading `K_DIV` reads whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines
